      "text": "OPENING (first 60 seconds — DO NOT draw yet):\n\"Before I start designing, let me make sure I understand the scope.\nAre we optimizing for [read-heavy / write-heavy]? What's our target\nDAU — millions or hundreds of millions? And do we need global\ndistribution or single-region? ... Great. I'll use those to anchor.\"\n\nPROPOSING EVERY COMPONENT (template):\n\"I'd add [component] here because [specific NFR it addresses].\nMy default choice is [technology A] — [one-line reason].\nWe could alternatively use [technology B], which gives us [benefit]\nat the cost of [trade-off]. Given our [NFR], I'll go with A.\"\n\nARTICULATING A BOTTLENECK:\n\"The concern with [component] is [specific failure mode].\nAt [scale metric] — say 35K RPS — [what breaks].\nTwo approaches: [Solution A] which gives us [benefit] but costs [X];\n[Solution B] which costs [Y] but gives us [Z].\nI'd recommend [A] because [tie to NFR from Step 1].\"\n\nPROACTIVE TRADE-OFF MENTION:\n\"I want to call out a trade-off: we're sacrificing [consistency /\nlatency / simplicity] in exchange for [availability / throughput /\nscale]. That's the right call here because [business reason].\"\n\nHANDLING \"WHY NOT X?\":\n\"Great question. [X] would work — the reason I didn't lead with it\nis [specific technical reason]. If [condition] changed, I'd reconsider.\"\n\nWRAP-UP:\n\"Let me summarize the key decisions: [1], [2], [3].\nThe biggest risk I see is [X], mitigated by [Y].\nIf I had another 30 minutes, I'd explore [Z] to improve [metric].\"\n\nSTAFF-LEVEL SIGNALS TO DROP IN NATURALLY:\n• Cost: \"Rough estimate: at this scale, that's ~$X/month.\n  The [component] saves us ~$Y/month on [resource].\"\n• Conway's Law: \"I'd structure service ownership so [team A] owns\n  [service X] end-to-end — API, DB schema, and on-call rotation.\"\n• Security: \"I'd put the DB in a private subnet — no public route,\n  only reachable from the service layer via security group rule.\"\n• Phased delivery: \"Phase 1 gets us to 10K users.\n  Phase 2 at 100K: we add [component]. Phase 3 at 1M: revisit [decision].\"\n• Operational: \"Two failure modes I'd want runbooks for: [X] and [Y].\"",
      "originalText": "OPENING (first 60 seconds — DO NOT draw yet):\n\"Before I start designing, let me make sure I understand the scope.\nAre we optimizing for [read-heavy / write-heavy]? What's our target\nDAU — millions or hundreds of millions? And do we need global\ndistribution or single-region? ... Great. I'll use those to anchor.\"\n\nPROPOSING EVERY COMPONENT (template):\n\"I'd add [component] here because [specific NFR it addresses].\nMy default choice is [technology A] — [one-line reason].\nWe could alternatively use [technology B], which gives us [benefit]\nat the cost of [trade-off]. Given our [NFR], I'll go with A.\"\n\nARTICULATING A BOTTLENECK:\n\"The concern with [component] is [specific failure mode].\nAt [scale metric] — say 35K RPS — [what breaks].\nTwo approaches: [Solution A] which gives us [benefit] but costs [X];\n[Solution B] which costs [Y] but gives us [Z].\nI'd recommend [A] because [tie to NFR from Step 1].\"\n\nPROACTIVE TRADE-OFF MENTION:\n\"I want to call out a trade-off: we're sacrificing [consistency /\nlatency / simplicity] in exchange for [availability / throughput /\nscale]. That's the right call here because [business reason].\"\n\nHANDLING \"WHY NOT X?\":\n\"Great question. [X] would work — the reason I didn't lead with it\nis [specific technical reason]. If [condition] changed, I'd reconsider.\"\n\nWRAP-UP:\n\"Let me summarize the key decisions: [1], [2], [3].\nThe biggest risk I see is [X], mitigated by [Y].\nIf I had another 30 minutes, I'd explore [Z] to improve [metric].\"\n\nSTAFF-LEVEL SIGNALS TO DROP IN NATURALLY:\n• Cost: \"Rough estimate: at this scale, that's ~$X/month.\n  The [component] saves us ~$Y/month on [resource].\"\n• Conway's Law: \"I'd structure service ownership so [team A] owns\n  [service X] end-to-end — API, DB schema, and on-call rotation.\"\n• Security: \"I'd put the DB in a private subnet — no public route,\n  only reachable from the service layer via security group rule.\"\n• Phased delivery: \"Phase 1 gets us to 10K users.\n  Phase 2 at 100K: we add [component]. Phase 3 at 1M: revisit [decision].\"\n• Operational: \"Two failure modes I'd want runbooks for: [X] and [Y].\"",
