      "text": "DATABASE TAXONOMY — pick by access pattern\n\nRELATIONAL (ACID):\n• PostgreSQL: JSONB, FTS, PostGIS, MVCC\n• Aurora: multi-AZ HA, read replicas\n• Use: relational data, joins, compliance\n\nKEY-VALUE (fastest reads/writes):\n• Redis: in-memory, pub/sub, sorted sets, streams\n• DynamoDB: serverless, GSI, single-digit ms, DAX\n• Use: sessions, cache, leaderboards, counters\n\nDOCUMENT (flexible schema):\n• MongoDB: aggregation, Atlas Search, nested docs\n• Firestore: real-time sync, offline first\n• Use: hierarchical, schema-evolving data\n\nCOLUMN-FAMILY (write-heavy, massive scale):\n• Cassandra: LSM-tree, tunable consistency, multi-DC\n• Use: >10M writes/day, time-series, known partition key\n\nSEARCH: Elasticsearch — inverted index, BM25,\n  autocomplete, faceted, percolate\nGRAPH: Neo4j — Cypher, relationship traversal\nTIME-SERIES: InfluxDB, TimescaleDB\n\nINDEXING\n• B-Tree: range + equality (default PG/MySQL)\n• LSM-Tree: write-optimized (Cassandra/RocksDB)\n• Inverted: full-text (Elasticsearch)\n• Composite: match query filter column order\n• Partial: WHERE is_active=true (smaller index)\n• Covering: include all SELECT cols (index-only scan)\n\nSHARDING\n• Hash: even distribution; no range queries\n• Range: ordered; hotspot risk at boundaries\n• Consistent hashing: virtual nodes, minimal resharding\n\nREPLICATION\n• Sync: strong consistency, write latency\n• Async: eventual, read scale, lag < 1s\n• Monitor: seconds_behind_master; alert > 5s",
      "originalText": "DATABASE TAXONOMY — pick by access pattern\n\nRELATIONAL (ACID):\n• PostgreSQL: JSONB, FTS, PostGIS, MVCC\n• Aurora: multi-AZ HA, read replicas\n• Use: relational data, joins, compliance\n\nKEY-VALUE (fastest reads/writes):\n• Redis: in-memory, pub/sub, sorted sets, streams\n• DynamoDB: serverless, GSI, single-digit ms, DAX\n• Use: sessions, cache, leaderboards, counters\n\nDOCUMENT (flexible schema):\n• MongoDB: aggregation, Atlas Search, nested docs\n• Firestore: real-time sync, offline first\n• Use: hierarchical, schema-evolving data\n\nCOLUMN-FAMILY (write-heavy, massive scale):\n• Cassandra: LSM-tree, tunable consistency, multi-DC\n• Use: >10M writes/day, time-series, known partition key\n\nSEARCH: Elasticsearch — inverted index, BM25,\n  autocomplete, faceted, percolate\nGRAPH: Neo4j — Cypher, relationship traversal\nTIME-SERIES: InfluxDB, TimescaleDB\n\nINDEXING\n• B-Tree: range + equality (default PG/MySQL)\n• LSM-Tree: write-optimized (Cassandra/RocksDB)\n• Inverted: full-text (Elasticsearch)\n• Composite: match query filter column order\n• Partial: WHERE is_active=true (smaller index)\n• Covering: include all SELECT cols (index-only scan)\n\nSHARDING\n• Hash: even distribution; no range queries\n• Range: ordered; hotspot risk at boundaries\n• Consistent hashing: virtual nodes, minimal resharding\n\nREPLICATION\n• Sync: strong consistency, write latency\n• Async: eventual, read scale, lag < 1s\n• Monitor: seconds_behind_master; alert > 5s",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
