      "text": "ARCHITECTURE EVOLUTION\nMonolith → Modular Monolith → Microservices\nConway's Law: org structure drives system structure\n\nMONOLITH\n+ Simple deploy, fast iteration, no network hops\n- Vertical scaling only, deploy coupling\nUse: team < 15, domain unclear, MVP stage\n\nMODULAR MONOLITH\n+ Module boundaries enforced in code\n+ Easy to extract to microservices later\nUse: team growing, clearer domains\n\nMICROSERVICES\n+ Independent deploy, polyglot, team autonomy\n+ Horizontal scale per service\n- Network latency, distributed tracing, complex local dev\nUse: org > 50 eng, distinct bounded contexts\n\nDDD — DOMAIN-DRIVEN DESIGN\n• Bounded Context: own model + DB + API\n• Aggregate: consistency boundary\n  (1 transaction = 1 aggregate root)\n• Domain Events: notify other contexts\n• Ubiquitous language: code = domain terms\n\nCQRS\n• Separate write model (commands, ACID)\n  from read model (queries, denormalized)\n• Use: read/write scaling mismatch, complex domain\n\nEVENT SOURCING\n• Append-only event log; replay = state\n+ Audit trail, time-travel, replay consumers\n- Projection complexity, schema evolution\n\nSAGA (distributed transactions without 2PC)\n• Choreography: services react to events (decoupled)\n• Orchestration: saga coordinator drives steps (clear)\n• Compensating txns: undo each completed step\n\nOTHER PATTERNS\n• BFF: one API adapter per client type\n• Strangler Fig: incremental monolith migration\n• Sidecar: co-deployed proxy (Envoy/Istio mTLS)",
      "originalText": "ARCHITECTURE EVOLUTION\nMonolith → Modular Monolith → Microservices\nConway's Law: org structure drives system structure\n\nMONOLITH\n+ Simple deploy, fast iteration, no network hops\n- Vertical scaling only, deploy coupling\nUse: team < 15, domain unclear, MVP stage\n\nMODULAR MONOLITH\n+ Module boundaries enforced in code\n+ Easy to extract to microservices later\nUse: team growing, clearer domains\n\nMICROSERVICES\n+ Independent deploy, polyglot, team autonomy\n+ Horizontal scale per service\n- Network latency, distributed tracing, complex local dev\nUse: org > 50 eng, distinct bounded contexts\n\nDDD — DOMAIN-DRIVEN DESIGN\n• Bounded Context: own model + DB + API\n• Aggregate: consistency boundary\n  (1 transaction = 1 aggregate root)\n• Domain Events: notify other contexts\n• Ubiquitous language: code = domain terms\n\nCQRS\n• Separate write model (commands, ACID)\n  from read model (queries, denormalized)\n• Use: read/write scaling mismatch, complex domain\n\nEVENT SOURCING\n• Append-only event log; replay = state\n+ Audit trail, time-travel, replay consumers\n- Projection complexity, schema evolution\n\nSAGA (distributed transactions without 2PC)\n• Choreography: services react to events (decoupled)\n• Orchestration: saga coordinator drives steps (clear)\n• Compensating txns: undo each completed step\n\nOTHER PATTERNS\n• BFF: one API adapter per client type\n• Strangler Fig: incremental monolith migration\n• Sidecar: co-deployed proxy (Envoy/Istio mTLS)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "b6H"
    },
