      "text": "COMPUTE — choose by traffic pattern\n• EC2/VMs: full control, stateful, GPU\n• ECS/K8s: containerized, HPA auto-scale\n• Lambda/Fargate: serverless, event-driven\n  Cold start: 100ms–1s; max 15min (Lambda)\n\nCACHING LAYERS\n• L1 in-process: Guava/Caffeine — nanoseconds\n• L2 distributed: Redis/Memcached — microseconds\n• L3 CDN: geo-edge — milliseconds\n\nCACHE WRITE PATTERNS\n• Cache-Aside: lazy, resilient, cold-start penalty\n• Write-Through: always fresh, write latency\n• Write-Behind: low-latency writes, loss on crash\n• Eviction: LRU (recency), LFU (frequency), TTL\n\nMESSAGE BROKERS\n• Kafka: durable log, replay, consumer groups\n  Partition key: entity_id (order per entity)\n  Retention: 7d default → replay for new consumers\n• SQS: managed, at-least-once, DLQ after N retries\n• RabbitMQ: AMQP, routing, acks, RPC\n• SNS: pub/sub fan-out → SQS/Lambda/HTTP\n\nAPI PATTERNS\n• REST: cacheable, stateless, versioning (v1/)\n• gRPC: protobuf, streaming, codegen, deadlines\n• GraphQL: DataLoader for N+1 batching\n\nRATE LIMITING\n• Token Bucket: capacity N, refill R — burst-friendly\n• Sliding Window Log: sorted set — precise\n• Fixed Window: INCR+EXPIRE — simple, edge-burst risk\n• Distributed: Redis Lua EVAL (atomic check+decrement)\n\nLOAD BALANCING\n• Round-robin: equal dist, stateless services\n• Least-connections: route to least-busy\n• IP-hash: sticky sessions per client IP\n• Health-check: auto-remove unhealthy instances",
      "originalText": "COMPUTE — choose by traffic pattern\n• EC2/VMs: full control, stateful, GPU\n• ECS/K8s: containerized, HPA auto-scale\n• Lambda/Fargate: serverless, event-driven\n  Cold start: 100ms–1s; max 15min (Lambda)\n\nCACHING LAYERS\n• L1 in-process: Guava/Caffeine — nanoseconds\n• L2 distributed: Redis/Memcached — microseconds\n• L3 CDN: geo-edge — milliseconds\n\nCACHE WRITE PATTERNS\n• Cache-Aside: lazy, resilient, cold-start penalty\n• Write-Through: always fresh, write latency\n• Write-Behind: low-latency writes, loss on crash\n• Eviction: LRU (recency), LFU (frequency), TTL\n\nMESSAGE BROKERS\n• Kafka: durable log, replay, consumer groups\n  Partition key: entity_id (order per entity)\n  Retention: 7d default → replay for new consumers\n• SQS: managed, at-least-once, DLQ after N retries\n• RabbitMQ: AMQP, routing, acks, RPC\n• SNS: pub/sub fan-out → SQS/Lambda/HTTP\n\nAPI PATTERNS\n• REST: cacheable, stateless, versioning (v1/)\n• gRPC: protobuf, streaming, codegen, deadlines\n• GraphQL: DataLoader for N+1 batching\n\nRATE LIMITING\n• Token Bucket: capacity N, refill R — burst-friendly\n• Sliding Window Log: sorted set — precise\n• Fixed Window: INCR+EXPIRE — simple, edge-burst risk\n• Distributed: Redis Lua EVAL (atomic check+decrement)\n\nLOAD BALANCING\n• Round-robin: equal dist, stateless services\n• Least-connections: route to least-busy\n• IP-hash: sticky sessions per client IP\n• Health-check: auto-remove unhealthy instances",
