      "updated": 1782833661609,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "CONTAINERIZATION\n• Docker: immutable artifacts, multi-stage builds\n• Kubernetes: HPA, PodDisruptionBudget, probes\n• Helm: K8s package manager, values-templating\n• Service Mesh: Istio/Linkerd — mTLS, circuit breaking\n\nCI/CD PIPELINE\nBuild → Unit Tests → Integration Tests\n→ SAST/DAST → Build+Scan Image\n→ Deploy Staging → Smoke Tests\n→ Deploy Prod → Synthetic Monitoring\n→ Rollback trigger on SLO breach\n\nDEPLOYMENT STRATEGIES\n• Blue-Green: instant cutover + rollback, 2× cost\n• Canary: % traffic to new version, expand on SLO health\n• Rolling: replace pods one-by-one; version skew risk\n• Feature Flags: deploy dark; enable per cohort\n\nINFRASTRUCTURE AS CODE\n• Terraform: multi-cloud, plan/apply, modules\n• CloudFormation: AWS-native, drift detection\n• Pulumi: TypeScript/Python/Go IaC\n• GitOps: ArgoCD/Flux — cluster state in Git\n\nOBSERVABILITY (3 pillars)\n• Metrics: Prometheus + Grafana\n  RED: Rate, Error rate, Duration per service\n  USE: Utilization, Saturation, Errors per resource\n• Logs: structured JSON, ELK or Grafana Loki\n  Always include trace_id, span_id, service, level\n  Never log PII, passwords, tokens raw\n• Traces: OpenTelemetry → Jaeger/Tempo\n  W3C TraceContext; sample 100% errors + 1% success\n• Alerting: SLO burn-rate (fast 5m + slow 6h windows)\n• Synthetic: probe every 60s from 3+ regions\n\nDISASTER RECOVERY\n• Backup/Restore: RTO = hours, cheapest\n• Pilot Light: scaled-down standby, RTO = 30min\n• Warm Standby: full-size standby, RTO = 5min\n• Active-Active: best RTO, highest cost",
      "originalText": "CONTAINERIZATION\n• Docker: immutable artifacts, multi-stage builds\n• Kubernetes: HPA, PodDisruptionBudget, probes\n• Helm: K8s package manager, values-templating\n• Service Mesh: Istio/Linkerd — mTLS, circuit breaking\n\nCI/CD PIPELINE\nBuild → Unit Tests → Integration Tests\n→ SAST/DAST → Build+Scan Image\n→ Deploy Staging → Smoke Tests\n→ Deploy Prod → Synthetic Monitoring\n→ Rollback trigger on SLO breach\n\nDEPLOYMENT STRATEGIES\n• Blue-Green: instant cutover + rollback, 2× cost\n• Canary: % traffic to new version, expand on SLO health\n• Rolling: replace pods one-by-one; version skew risk\n• Feature Flags: deploy dark; enable per cohort\n\nINFRASTRUCTURE AS CODE\n• Terraform: multi-cloud, plan/apply, modules\n• CloudFormation: AWS-native, drift detection\n• Pulumi: TypeScript/Python/Go IaC\n• GitOps: ArgoCD/Flux — cluster state in Git\n\nOBSERVABILITY (3 pillars)\n• Metrics: Prometheus + Grafana\n  RED: Rate, Error rate, Duration per service\n  USE: Utilization, Saturation, Errors per resource\n• Logs: structured JSON, ELK or Grafana Loki\n  Always include trace_id, span_id, service, level\n  Never log PII, passwords, tokens raw\n• Traces: OpenTelemetry → Jaeger/Tempo\n  W3C TraceContext; sample 100% errors + 1% success\n• Alerting: SLO burn-rate (fast 5m + slow 6h windows)\n• Synthetic: probe every 60s from 3+ regions\n\nDISASTER RECOVERY\n• Backup/Restore: RTO = hours, cheapest\n• Pilot Light: scaled-down standby, RTO = 30min\n• Warm Standby: full-size standby, RTO = 5min\n• Active-Active: best RTO, highest cost",
