      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "AUTHENTICATION & AUTHORIZATION\nAuthN (who are you?):\n• OAuth2 + OIDC: federated SSO\n• JWT: stateless, verify sig + exp\n• Session tokens: server-side, revocable\nAuthZ (what can you do?):\n• RBAC: role-based — simple, coarse\n• ABAC: attribute-based — flexible, complex\n• ReBAC: relationship-based (Zanzibar)\n\nSECRETS MANAGEMENT\n• Never plaintext in code or env files\n• AWS Secrets Manager / HashiCorp Vault\n• Rotate automatically; audit all access\n• SOPS: encrypt secrets in Git\n\nTRANSPORT & ENCRYPTION\n• TLS 1.3 everywhere (internal + external)\n• mTLS: service-to-service (zero-trust)\n• Certificate pinning: mobile MITM prevention\n• At-rest: KMS envelope encryption\n• Field-level: PII/PCI columns in DB\n\nINPUT VALIDATION\n• OWASP Top 10: SQLi, XSS, CSRF, SSRF\n• Parameterized queries always\n• CSP headers, CORS allowlist (no wildcard)\n• Rate limit + CAPTCHA on public endpoints\n\nNETWORK SECURITY\n• VPC: private subnets for DB + internal svc\n• Security groups: deny by default\n• WAF: OWASP rules + geo-block + bot detect\n• DDoS: CloudFront+Shield or Cloudflare\n• Zero-trust: authenticate every hop\n\nCOMPLIANCE CONTROLS\n• GDPR: EU data residency, right to erasure, DPA\n• HIPAA: PHI encryption + audit logs + BAA\n• PCI-DSS: tokenization, quarterly scan\n• SOC 2: audit logs, access controls, change mgmt\n\nSECURITY IN SDLC\n• SAST: SonarQube/Semgrep in CI\n• DAST: OWASP ZAP in staging\n• Dependency scan: Snyk / Dependabot\n• Threat modeling: STRIDE per feature\n• Pen test: quarterly external + bug bounty",
      "originalText": "AUTHENTICATION & AUTHORIZATION\nAuthN (who are you?):\n• OAuth2 + OIDC: federated SSO\n• JWT: stateless, verify sig + exp\n• Session tokens: server-side, revocable\nAuthZ (what can you do?):\n• RBAC: role-based — simple, coarse\n• ABAC: attribute-based — flexible, complex\n• ReBAC: relationship-based (Zanzibar)\n\nSECRETS MANAGEMENT\n• Never plaintext in code or env files\n• AWS Secrets Manager / HashiCorp Vault\n• Rotate automatically; audit all access\n• SOPS: encrypt secrets in Git\n\nTRANSPORT & ENCRYPTION\n• TLS 1.3 everywhere (internal + external)\n• mTLS: service-to-service (zero-trust)\n• Certificate pinning: mobile MITM prevention\n• At-rest: KMS envelope encryption\n• Field-level: PII/PCI columns in DB\n\nINPUT VALIDATION\n• OWASP Top 10: SQLi, XSS, CSRF, SSRF\n• Parameterized queries always\n• CSP headers, CORS allowlist (no wildcard)\n• Rate limit + CAPTCHA on public endpoints\n\nNETWORK SECURITY\n• VPC: private subnets for DB + internal svc\n• Security groups: deny by default\n• WAF: OWASP rules + geo-block + bot detect\n• DDoS: CloudFront+Shield or Cloudflare\n• Zero-trust: authenticate every hop\n\nCOMPLIANCE CONTROLS\n• GDPR: EU data residency, right to erasure, DPA\n• HIPAA: PHI encryption + audit logs + BAA\n• PCI-DSS: tokenization, quarterly scan\n• SOC 2: audit logs, access controls, change mgmt\n\nSECURITY IN SDLC\n• SAST: SonarQube/Semgrep in CI\n• DAST: OWASP ZAP in staging\n• Dependency scan: Snyk / Dependabot\n• Threat modeling: STRIDE per feature\n• Pen test: quarterly external + bug bounty",
