      "updated": 1782833663392,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "CDN\n• Fingerprinted filenames → Cache-Control: immutable, max-age=31536000\n• API responses: Surrogate-Control: max-age=60, stale-while-revalidate=30\n• Origin shield: single PoP → reduces origin hits 10–30×\n• Providers: CloudFront (AWS), Cloudflare (DDoS+WAF), Fastly (real-time config)\n• Skip CDN: user-specific data, write paths, regulated data residency\n\nLOAD BALANCER\n• L7 ALB: host/path routing, SSL termination, WebSocket upgrade\n• L4 NLB: ultra-low latency, no HTTP context — gaming, DB proxy\n• Health: active (/health HTTP) + passive (5xx rate tracking)\n• Connection draining: 30s grace before removing unhealthy instance\n• Avoid sticky sessions: use Redis for sessions → stateless LB\n\nAPI GATEWAY\n• Responsibilities: auth, rate limit, routing, SSL, transform, logging\n• Managed: AWS API GW (pay-per-call) | Self-hosted: Kong, Traefik\n• Anti-pattern: business logic in gateway (gateway = infrastructure only)\n• Rate limit: token bucket in Redis, return 429 + Retry-After header\n• Circuit breaker at gateway → prevents cascade to all downstream services\n\nCACHE (Redis)\n• Key design: namespace:type:id (user:profile:123) → enables pattern delete\n• TTL: shorter = fresh | longer = DB relief; stale-while-revalidate pattern\n• Thundering herd: probabilistic early expiry OR mutex on first miss\n• Hot key: key + rand(0, N) → distribute reads across N virtual shards\n• Redis Cluster: 16384 hash slots, auto failover; cross-slot ops restricted\n• Do NOT cache: financial real-time data, low-read-frequency entities\n\nMESSAGE QUEUE\n• Kafka: ordered per partition, durable log, replay up to N months\n  Partition key = entity_id (preserves ordering per entity)\n  Consumer group = horizontal scale (up to partition count)\n• SQS: visibility timeout > max processing time; DLQ after N retries\n• Idempotency: consumer MUST store processed event_ids before processing\n• Outbox pattern: write event + state in same DB tx → relay publishes\n  Eliminates dual-write inconsistency between state and event store",
      "originalText": "CDN\n• Fingerprinted filenames → Cache-Control: immutable, max-age=31536000\n• API responses: Surrogate-Control: max-age=60, stale-while-revalidate=30\n• Origin shield: single PoP → reduces origin hits 10–30×\n• Providers: CloudFront (AWS), Cloudflare (DDoS+WAF), Fastly (real-time config)\n• Skip CDN: user-specific data, write paths, regulated data residency\n\nLOAD BALANCER\n• L7 ALB: host/path routing, SSL termination, WebSocket upgrade\n• L4 NLB: ultra-low latency, no HTTP context — gaming, DB proxy\n• Health: active (/health HTTP) + passive (5xx rate tracking)\n• Connection draining: 30s grace before removing unhealthy instance\n• Avoid sticky sessions: use Redis for sessions → stateless LB\n\nAPI GATEWAY\n• Responsibilities: auth, rate limit, routing, SSL, transform, logging\n• Managed: AWS API GW (pay-per-call) | Self-hosted: Kong, Traefik\n• Anti-pattern: business logic in gateway (gateway = infrastructure only)\n• Rate limit: token bucket in Redis, return 429 + Retry-After header\n• Circuit breaker at gateway → prevents cascade to all downstream services\n\nCACHE (Redis)\n• Key design: namespace:type:id (user:profile:123) → enables pattern delete\n• TTL: shorter = fresh | longer = DB relief; stale-while-revalidate pattern\n• Thundering herd: probabilistic early expiry OR mutex on first miss\n• Hot key: key + rand(0, N) → distribute reads across N virtual shards\n• Redis Cluster: 16384 hash slots, auto failover; cross-slot ops restricted\n• Do NOT cache: financial real-time data, low-read-frequency entities\n\nMESSAGE QUEUE\n• Kafka: ordered per partition, durable log, replay up to N months\n  Partition key = entity_id (preserves ordering per entity)\n  Consumer group = horizontal scale (up to partition count)\n• SQS: visibility timeout > max processing time; DLQ after N retries\n• Idempotency: consumer MUST store processed event_ids before processing\n• Outbox pattern: write event + state in same DB tx → relay publishes\n  Eliminates dual-write inconsistency between state and event store",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
