    {
      "id": "g3BPRightBody",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2254.5160667516016,
      "y": 6622.747824369484,
      "width": 783.4346561552052,
      "height": 900,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "HnMfl3zUaLJez2eI6LWk",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 3049,
      "version": 559,
      "versionNonce": 1213153115,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1782833663392,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "DATABASE\n• Connection pool: PgBouncer (PG), ProxySQL (MySQL)\n  Pool size = (cores × 2) + disk spindle count (empirical rule)\n• Read replicas: route 80% of reads; monitor lag (alert >5s)\n• EXPLAIN ANALYZE: every query >100ms; cover WHERE + ORDER BY cols\n• Partial index: WHERE is_active = true (smaller, faster, targeted)\n• Expand-contract migration: add nullable → backfill → add constraint\n  (zero-downtime; never add NOT NULL to existing table directly)\n• N+1: detect via log_min_duration_statement; fix with JOINs or DataLoader\n\nOBSERVABILITY\n• Metrics (RED per service): Rate, Error rate, Duration P50/P99\n• Metrics (USE per infra): Utilization, Saturation, Errors\n• SLO alerts: burn-rate (fast 5m + slow 6h windows) > threshold alerts\n• Logs: structured JSON; always include trace_id, span_id, service, level\n  Never log raw: passwords, tokens, PII fields\n• Traces: OpenTelemetry → Jaeger/Tempo; W3C TraceContext headers\n  Sample: 100% of errors + 1% of success traces (cost control)\n• Synthetic: probe golden-path every 60s from 3+ regions\n\nSERVICE-TO-SERVICE\n• Sync (gRPC): set deadline on every call (never infinite wait)\n  Retry only idempotent calls; non-idempotent needs idempotency-key\n• Async (Kafka/SQS): producer fires-and-forgets; consumer idempotent\n• Timeout hierarchy: outer client deadline → propagate through each hop\n  Never set inner timeout longer than outer (wasted work)\n• mTLS: zero-trust; Istio/Linkerd service mesh automates cert rotation\n• Service discovery: K8s DNS (in-cluster), Consul (multi-cluster/cloud)\n\nSECURITY BASELINE (every production system)\n• All DBs in private subnets (no public route, SG from svc layer only)\n• All secrets in Secrets Manager / Vault (never plaintext in env vars)\n• TLS 1.3 everywhere; mTLS between internal services\n• WAF in front of CDN (OWASP managed rules, DDoS protection)\n• Audit logs: every data-access event with actor, resource, timestamp\n• Zero-trust: no implicit trust even on internal network — verify every hop",
      "originalText": "DATABASE\n• Connection pool: PgBouncer (PG), ProxySQL (MySQL)\n  Pool size = (cores × 2) + disk spindle count (empirical rule)\n• Read replicas: route 80% of reads; monitor lag (alert >5s)\n• EXPLAIN ANALYZE: every query >100ms; cover WHERE + ORDER BY cols\n• Partial index: WHERE is_active = true (smaller, faster, targeted)\n• Expand-contract migration: add nullable → backfill → add constraint\n  (zero-downtime; never add NOT NULL to existing table directly)\n• N+1: detect via log_min_duration_statement; fix with JOINs or DataLoader\n\nOBSERVABILITY\n• Metrics (RED per service): Rate, Error rate, Duration P50/P99\n• Metrics (USE per infra): Utilization, Saturation, Errors\n• SLO alerts: burn-rate (fast 5m + slow 6h windows) > threshold alerts\n• Logs: structured JSON; always include trace_id, span_id, service, level\n  Never log raw: passwords, tokens, PII fields\n• Traces: OpenTelemetry → Jaeger/Tempo; W3C TraceContext headers\n  Sample: 100% of errors + 1% of success traces (cost control)\n• Synthetic: probe golden-path every 60s from 3+ regions\n\nSERVICE-TO-SERVICE\n• Sync (gRPC): set deadline on every call (never infinite wait)\n  Retry only idempotent calls; non-idempotent needs idempotency-key\n• Async (Kafka/SQS): producer fires-and-forgets; consumer idempotent\n• Timeout hierarchy: outer client deadline → propagate through each hop\n  Never set inner timeout longer than outer (wasted work)\n• mTLS: zero-trust; Istio/Linkerd service mesh automates cert rotation\n• Service discovery: K8s DNS (in-cluster), Consul (multi-cluster/cloud)\n\nSECURITY BASELINE (every production system)\n• All DBs in private subnets (no public route, SG from svc layer only)\n• All secrets in Secrets Manager / Vault (never plaintext in env vars)\n• TLS 1.3 everywhere; mTLS between internal services\n• WAF in front of CDN (OWASP managed rules, DDoS protection)\n• Audit logs: every data-access event with actor, resource, timestamp\n• Zero-trust: no implicit trust even on internal network — verify every hop",
