      "seed": 3055,
      "version": 375,
      "versionNonce": 1159511835,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1782833663392,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "TECHNOLOGY SELECTION REFERENCE",
      "originalText": "TECHNOLOGY SELECTION REFERENCE",
      "fontSize": 34.06,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "b7I"
    },
    {
      "id": "g3TechLeftBdy",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 627.0887986416005,
      "y": 9480.243484757293,
      "width": 1650,
      "height": 825,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "HnMfl3zUaLJez2eI6LWk",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 3056,
      "version": 420,
      "versionNonce": 1191977915,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1782833663392,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "API STYLE — when to choose\n• REST: public APIs, CRUD, HTTP caching, browser clients\n• gRPC: internal microservices, high-perf, streaming, codegen\n• GraphQL: mobile-first, multiple client types, client-driven queries\n• WebSocket: bidirectional real-time (chat, live feeds, games)\n• SSE: server→client streaming (notifications, dashboards)\n\nDATABASE SELECTION FRAMEWORK\nStep 1 — Access pattern?\n  • Simple key lookups → Redis / DynamoDB\n  • Relational joins, ACID → PostgreSQL / Aurora\n  • Full-text search → Elasticsearch\n  • Time-series → InfluxDB / TimescaleDB\n  • Graph traversal → Neo4j\n  • Write-heavy time-series, no JOINs → Cassandra\nStep 2 — Write:read ratio?\n  • Read-heavy (>10:1 R:W) → add cache + read replicas\n  • Write-heavy (>10:1 W:R) → LSM-tree DB (Cassandra)\n  • Balanced → B-tree DB with read replicas\nStep 3 — Consistency requirement?\n  • Strong ACID → SQL\n  • Eventual, multi-region → Cassandra / DynamoDB\nStep 4 — Scale target?\n  • <10M records, <10K RPS → any SQL DB works fine\n  • 10M–1B records → sharding or managed (Aurora, DynamoDB)\n  • >1B records → Cassandra, Bigtable, or sharded SQL\n\nCOMPUTE SELECTION\n• EC2/VM: full control, stateful, GPU, predictable cost\n• ECS + Fargate: managed containers, AWS native\n• Kubernetes: max portability, complex, large platform teams\n• Lambda: event-driven, zero ops, 15min max, cold starts\n• App Runner: simple web apps, low-ops teams",
      "originalText": "API STYLE — when to choose\n• REST: public APIs, CRUD, HTTP caching, browser clients\n• gRPC: internal microservices, high-perf, streaming, codegen\n• GraphQL: mobile-first, multiple client types, client-driven queries\n• WebSocket: bidirectional real-time (chat, live feeds, games)\n• SSE: server→client streaming (notifications, dashboards)\n\nDATABASE SELECTION FRAMEWORK\nStep 1 — Access pattern?\n  • Simple key lookups → Redis / DynamoDB\n  • Relational joins, ACID → PostgreSQL / Aurora\n  • Full-text search → Elasticsearch\n  • Time-series → InfluxDB / TimescaleDB\n  • Graph traversal → Neo4j\n  • Write-heavy time-series, no JOINs → Cassandra\nStep 2 — Write:read ratio?\n  • Read-heavy (>10:1 R:W) → add cache + read replicas\n  • Write-heavy (>10:1 W:R) → LSM-tree DB (Cassandra)\n  • Balanced → B-tree DB with read replicas\nStep 3 — Consistency requirement?\n  • Strong ACID → SQL\n  • Eventual, multi-region → Cassandra / DynamoDB\nStep 4 — Scale target?\n  • <10M records, <10K RPS → any SQL DB works fine\n  • 10M–1B records → sharding or managed (Aurora, DynamoDB)\n  • >1B records → Cassandra, Bigtable, or sharded SQL\n\nCOMPUTE SELECTION\n• EC2/VM: full control, stateful, GPU, predictable cost\n• ECS + Fargate: managed containers, AWS native\n• Kubernetes: max portability, complex, large platform teams\n• Lambda: event-driven, zero ops, 15min max, cold starts\n• App Runner: simple web apps, low-ops teams",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "b7J"
    },
    {
      "id": "g3TechRgtBdy1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2299.2552953342915,
      "y": 9452.147529564785,
      "width": 1650,
      "height": 925,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "HnMfl3zUaLJez2eI6LWk",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 3057,
      "version": 424,
      "versionNonce": 1793455195,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1782833663392,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "SCALING PROGRESSION (do in order)\n1. Index optimization (EXPLAIN ANALYZE, free)\n2. Query optimization (JOIN instead of N+1)\n3. Connection pooling (PgBouncer/ProxySQL)\n4. Caching layer (Redis, target 80%+ hit rate)\n5. Read replicas (route 80% of reads)\n6. Vertical scaling (larger instance, simpler)\n7. Sharding (last resort; highest complexity cost)\n8. DB type change (if access pattern fundamentally different)\n\nFAILURE PATTERNS & MITIGATIONS\nThundering herd:\n  → Probabilistic early expiry + request coalescing\nSplit-brain (two primaries after partition):\n  → Quorum writes (majority must ack) + fencing tokens\nCascading failure:\n  → Timeout + circuit breaker + bulkhead\nHot partition (write hotspot):\n  → Random suffix on partition key + write sharding\nSlow consumer (queue lag growing):\n  → Scale consumers (up to partition count) + DLQ\nRetry storm:\n  → Exponential backoff + full jitter + max deadline\n\nDISASTER RECOVERY\n• RPO: max data loss → dictates backup frequency\n• RTO: max downtime → dictates failover automation\n• Backup/Restore: hours RTO, cheapest\n• Pilot Light: minutes RTO, minimal standby\n• Warm Standby: ~5min RTO, full-size standby\n• Active-Active: <1min RTO, highest cost\n\nGLOBAL DISTRIBUTION\n• Active-Active: all regions write, conflict resolution required\n• Active-Passive: one primary, failover to secondary (simpler)\n• Geo-routing: Route53 latency routing → nearest region\n• Data residency: GDPR → EU users must stay in EU region",
      "originalText": "SCALING PROGRESSION (do in order)\n1. Index optimization (EXPLAIN ANALYZE, free)\n2. Query optimization (JOIN instead of N+1)\n3. Connection pooling (PgBouncer/ProxySQL)\n4. Caching layer (Redis, target 80%+ hit rate)\n5. Read replicas (route 80% of reads)\n6. Vertical scaling (larger instance, simpler)\n7. Sharding (last resort; highest complexity cost)\n8. DB type change (if access pattern fundamentally different)\n\nFAILURE PATTERNS & MITIGATIONS\nThundering herd:\n  → Probabilistic early expiry + request coalescing\nSplit-brain (two primaries after partition):\n  → Quorum writes (majority must ack) + fencing tokens\nCascading failure:\n  → Timeout + circuit breaker + bulkhead\nHot partition (write hotspot):\n  → Random suffix on partition key + write sharding\nSlow consumer (queue lag growing):\n  → Scale consumers (up to partition count) + DLQ\nRetry storm:\n  → Exponential backoff + full jitter + max deadline\n\nDISASTER RECOVERY\n• RPO: max data loss → dictates backup frequency\n• RTO: max downtime → dictates failover automation\n• Backup/Restore: hours RTO, cheapest\n• Pilot Light: minutes RTO, minimal standby\n• Warm Standby: ~5min RTO, full-size standby\n• Active-Active: <1min RTO, highest cost\n\nGLOBAL DISTRIBUTION\n• Active-Active: all regions write, conflict resolution required\n• Active-Passive: one primary, failover to secondary (simpler)\n• Geo-routing: Route53 latency routing → nearest region\n• Data residency: GDPR → EU users must stay in EU region",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "b7K"
    },
